Show the Cloud console and its CLI, not just the marketing page

The asmdb Cloud section carried only the homepage, which says what the
service is but not what using it looks like. Two captures fill that in:
the Database view, where rows and live stats come from the instance
itself, and the CLI tab, which accepts the same commands as the local
binary against a hosted database.

Both are placed against the paragraphs they illustrate rather than
grouped as a gallery, so a reader meets each one where the text has just
made a claim about it.

